@startuml Sequence_Purchase_Reservation
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
autonumber

title SALESTORM – Purchase / Reservation Sequence ("Buy Now")\nincludes: success · duplicate request · sold out · last-unit race

actor Customer as C
participant "CDN/WAF" as CDN
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Waiting Room" as WR
participant "Inventory Service\n(ReservationService)" as INV
database "Redis\n(stock gate)" as R
database "Inventory DB\n(PostgreSQL)" as DB
queue "Kafka" as K

C -> CDN : POST /v1/sales/{saleId}/reservations\nAuthorization: Bearer JWT\nIdempotency-Key: k-123
CDN -> CDN : bot score / WAF rules
CDN -> GW : forward
GW -> GW : verify JWT, rate limit (5 req/s/user)
alt waiting room active
  GW -> WR : request admission
  WR --> C : 202 queued (position N)
  ...client polls; admitted at controlled rate...
  WR --> GW : signed admission token (TTL 60 s)
end
GW -> INV : reserve(saleId, customerId, qty=1, key=k-123)

== Step A – Idempotency check ==
INV -> R : GET idem:k-123
alt key already seen (duplicate click / client retry)
  R --> INV : reservationId R-77
  INV --> C : 200 OK (same reservation R-77, replayed)
else new request
  R --> INV : nil

== Step B – Fast gate (atomic Lua, single-threaded in Redis) ==
  INV -> R : EVALSHA reserve.lua\n KEYS: stock:{sale}, buyers:{sale}, idem:k-123\n ARGV: customerId, qty=1
  note right of R
    if SISMEMBER buyers customer -> return ALREADY_BOUGHT
    if GET stock < qty          -> return SOLD_OUT
    DECRBY stock qty
    SADD buyers customer
    SET idem:k-123 PENDING EX 900
    return OK
  end note
  alt SOLD_OUT (≈ 9,900 of 10,000 requests)
    R --> INV : SOLD_OUT
    INV --> C : 409 Conflict {code: SOLD_OUT}  (< 50 ms)
  else ALREADY_BOUGHT (per-customer limit)
    R --> INV : ALREADY_BOUGHT
    INV --> C : 409 Conflict {code: LIMIT_REACHED}
  else OK (≤ 100 requests)
    R --> INV : OK

== Step C – Source of truth (ONE local ACID transaction) ==
    INV -> DB : BEGIN
    INV -> DB : UPDATE inventory\n SET available_quantity = available_quantity - 1,\n     reserved_quantity  = reserved_quantity + 1,\n     version = version + 1, updated_at = now()\n WHERE sale_id = :sale AND available_quantity >= 1
    alt 1 row updated
      INV -> DB : INSERT inventory_reservation\n (id, sale_id, customer_id, qty, status='RESERVED',\n  idempotency_key='k-123', expires_at = now()+10 min)
      INV -> DB : INSERT outbox_event (reservation.created)
      INV -> DB : COMMIT
      INV -> R : SET idem:k-123 R-77 EX 900
      INV --> C : 201 Created {reservationId: R-77, expiresAt}
      DB --> K : outbox relay → reservation.created
    else 0 rows (DB says no stock) OR unique violation (duplicate key)
      INV -> DB : ROLLBACK
      INV -> R : compensate: INCRBY stock 1, SREM buyers customer
      INV --> C : 409 SOLD_OUT  /  200 existing reservation
    end
  end
end

note over INV, DB
  **Last-unit race:** two requests reach Inventory at the same time with 1 unit left.
  Redis executes Lua scripts one at a time → only one sees stock=1; the other sees 0 → SOLD_OUT.
  Even if Redis were wrong, PostgreSQL row lock + "WHERE available_quantity >= 1"
  + CHECK (available_quantity >= 0) lets exactly ONE update succeed.
end note
@enduml
